    "note": "Version read: introduced, as filed (document 23-1023-02000). Failed on Senate second reading, yeas 21 nays 25, 2023-02-08. Section 1 amends 62.1-02-05, so struck and added words run together. Which of subsection 1(b) and 1(c) are kept is unclear, and the opening of subsection 6 (\"violates this section ... infraction\" versus \"subdivision a of subsection 1\") shows strike and add run together; the penalty is quoted only in its plainly new class A and class B parts. Words in subsections 1 and 6 may be struck; check the page image. Not quoted: the many exemptions in subsection 2 (except (l) and (p)), kept for context."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(1)): An individual may not possess a firearm or dangerous weapon at:\nSection 1 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(1)(a)): A school or school-sponsored event on school property;\nSection 1 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(2)(l)): An individual in a publicly owned or operated rest area or restroom;\nSection 1 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(2)(p)): An individual authorized to carry a concealed weapon on school property under section 62.1-02-14.\nSection 1 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(6)(a)): A class A misdemeanor if the individual is in possession of a firearm.\nSection 1 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(6)(b)): A class B misdemeanor if the individual is in possession of a dangerous weapon."
}